                <pb facs="0937" n="817" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg817"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00 Bandit Activities, 1931/01: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-21T17:00:00-05:45">April 21, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:28 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>36. The Department’s April 20, 1 p.m. The Jefe Director of the National Guard has
                    informed me that 18 enlisted Guardia were safely transported by marine airplane
                    to Puerto Cabezas today.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
